  "answer": "### Short Answer\nYes, a self-employed individual with gross sales below ₱3 million can opt for the 8% income tax rate, provided their gross sales or gross receipts do not exceed the VAT threshold of ₱3 million.\n\n### Controlling Authorities\nThe relevant provision is found in Section 24(B)(1)(b) of the National Internal Revenue Code (NIRC), which allows self-employed individuals and professionals to choose an 8% tax on gross sales or gross receipts exceeding ₱250,000 in lieu of the graduated income tax rates.\n\n### Interpretation\nUnder the NIRC, self-employed individuals whose gross sales or receipts do not exceed the VAT threshold (₱3 million) can avail themselves of the 8% income tax rate. This option is available as long as their gross income exceeds ₱250,000, which is the minimum threshold for taxation under this scheme.\n\n### Practical Meaning\nThis provision provides a simplified tax regime for small businesses, allowing them to pay a flat rate of 8% on their income above ₱250,000 instead of following the more complex graduated tax rates. This can significantly reduce the tax burden and simplify compliance for self-employed individuals and small business owners.",
